          "claim_id": "imp-1",
          "judge": null,
          "text": "Bispecific and antibody-drug-conjugate regimens moving into newly diagnosed, transplant-ineligible populations would shift myeloma treatment volume earlier in the pathway and toward outpatient infusion capacity. CRS and neurotoxicity monitoring requirements imply step-up dosing capacity and staff training that community sites do not uniformly have today."
        }
      ],
